<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  MechanoidRaids_PlanetWideDeny.xml       UtinniPatches - new file 2026-09-10
  ============================================================================
  MECH_PRESENCE_ENFORCEMENT_1, piece 3/4. Enforces the RATIFIED planet-wide
  axis-3 doctrine (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/mechanoid_biome_presence_draft.md,
  "Planet-wide doctrine for axis 3", owner 2026-09-10): random mechanoid RAIDS
  are DENY everywhere. Mechanoid violence reaches the player only as
  scripted/provoked response (Cathedral trespass, war-lab breach, Deeps
  mining, Forge/Scald tower assault) - never a storyteller-rolled raid.

  VERIFIED before writing (rimsage read_csharp_symbol/get_def_details, 2026-09-10):
  - The raid-faction weighting chain
    (`IncidentWorker_RaidEnemy.TryResolveRaidFaction` ->
    `PawnGroupMakerUtility.TryGetRandomFactionForCombatPawnGroupWeighted` ->
    `FactionCanBeGroupSource`) weights candidate factions by
    `f.def.RaidCommonalityFromPoints(points)` - no BiomeDef reference
    anywhere, confirmed by the spec's own verification pass (cited in its
    MECHANISM section). Zeroing this curve on the mechanoid FactionDef kills
    random-raid selection globally, in XML, with no biome-scoping needed.
  - The exact field, confirmed on the LIVE def via `get_def_details`
    (defType FactionDef, defName `Mechanoid`, label "mechanoid hive"/
    "the Forgotten Arsenal" per this campaign's own faction-lore patch):
      <raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
        <points>
          <li>(300,  0)</li>
          <li>(700,  1)</li>
          <li>(1400, 1.8)</li>
          <li>(2800, 2.2)</li>
          <li>(4000, 2.6)</li>
        </points>
      </raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
    This is `SimpleCurve`, not a plain float - "zero the curve" means every
    point's commonality collapses to 0, not deleting the field (an absent/
    empty curve is a different failure mode - RaidCommonalityFromPoints on an
    empty curve is undefined/0-length, where a single (0,0) point is an
    explicit, always-0 curve).
  - Only ONE FactionDef in the live def dump both looks mechanoid-flavoured
    and carries a `raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve`: `Mechanoid` itself
    (checked every FactionDef with a non-empty curve for "mech" in defName
    or label - one hit). No second mechanoid-adjacent raid faction exists to
    zero alongside it.
  - `earliestRaidDays`, `permanentEnemy`, `hostileToFactionlessHumanlikes`,
    `pawnGroupMakers` (used by scripted mech-cluster/site-defense content,
    NOT by the random-raid weighting chain above) are all left untouched -
    this patch only removes the RANDOM-RAID selection weight, exactly the
    doctrine's scope. Scripted/provoked mechanoid violence (mech clusters,
    site defenders, quest content) is unaffected.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Mechanoid"]/raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve</xpath>

    <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
      <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Mechanoid"]/raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve/points</xpath>
      <value>
        <points>
          <li>(0,0)</li>
        </points>
      </value>
    </match>

    <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="Mechanoid"]</xpath>
      <value>
        <raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
          <points>
            <li>(0,0)</li>
          </points>
        </raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
      </value>
    </nomatch>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
